Z||000000||frontal lobe||06-26-2000||11:14 PM||||OK, I kept HOPING that this topic would come up so I wouldn't have to be the one to ask it.  When I got the car it didn't have an owner's manual with it.  So could anyone please tell me:  HOW DO I SET THE STUPID CLOCK???????  I fiddled around and got the radio pre-sets, but can't crack the top-secret clock-setting code.  I suppose I could have just waited for day-light savings time to change again and save myself the embarrassment and potential ridicule, but here it is.  Anyone willing to help?  If so, you may go ahead and make your best wise-crack first, if you wish.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||06-26-2000||11:27 PM||||Simple enough.  You just need to purchase another Fiero - one with its clock set to standard time; leave your current vehicle set to daylight saving time.  Drive one car for six months, then switch to the other car, etc...<P>If you can't find/afford such a car, you need to move to Indiana.  They don't change their clocks (Hoosiers are smarter than the rest of the country). <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>All right...   (I think) mine goes something like this:<P>Turn ignition on.  Turn off radio.  Press SET button.  Press SCAN button until correct hour shows.  Press SEEK button until correct minute shows.<P>Press SET again.  You're done     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<P>Another little tidbit: If you want to see what time it is w/o turning ignition on, press the volume control knob.  I didn't know about this feature for years!  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Phaeton||06-27-2000||01:23 AM||||What is wrong with summer time year round?<P>Mine is same as above except tune up for hours and tune down for minutes.<P>What radio you got?  I got an analog clock out of an eagle for sale cheep.  Just twist the knob clockwise to set ahead, counter-clockwise to set back.  Oh yeah, push knob while turning.||||reg||12
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||06-27-2000||02:31 AM||||disconnect the battery, wait until 12, and hook it back up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-27-2000||02:36 AM||||Dang it!!! I was reading some threads and missed hooking up the battery at 12:00. Now I have to wait another 12 hours!!! (J/K)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000005||Patrick||06-27-2000||03:27 AM||||<BR>Move to a time zone that matches the reading on your clock... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||06-27-2000||03:56 AM||||Radio?? You guys have radios in your car?? Man....It must be nice to be rich..||||reg||8
