Z||000013||frontal lobe||06-27-2000||07:00 PM||||StuGood, excellent advice.  Sometimes the obvious solution is right in front of you, and you just can't see it!  I actually DO have 2 Fieros, but only one is running so...<P>Phaeton, good point but then I have to subtract by 1 WHILE DRIVING!!  I could probably handle all that if I had an automatic, but with all the activity going on in a 5-speed, well, that's just asking for overload.<P>Regarding moving to Indiana, my real first experience there was applying to Butler U. for college.  Man, were they SNOBBY!!!  By the time I figured out the whole state wasn't that way, I was living in Wisconsin.<P>FieroSTETZ, if I use the disconnect, connect battery method, is that 12 noon or 12 midnight???  Also, do you think I should do a battery relocation to the front of the car first to make it easier??<P>Patrick, excellent advice, but with the times changes I would have to buy 2 homes.  I'd rather have two running Fieros, although I don't know which would be cheaper to keep up.<P>Formula, if you do achieve going  back in time, could you pick me up a fiero owner's manual?  If not, Tom, I am listening, too.<P>Great news.  The StuGood method worked.  My car now has the correct time.  I swear it runs better now, too.<P>Thanks, everyone, for the excellent ideas and advice.<BR>||||reg||1
